      "text": " \n\nIn the diagram, we are given that $RSP$ is a straight line and $\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ$. We are asked to find the measure of $\\angle PQR$.\n\nTo find $\\angle PQR$, we first need to find $\\angle QRS$. This is because $RSP$ is a straight line and $\\angle QRS$ and $\\angle QSP$ together form a straight angle (180 degrees). So, we can find $\\angle QRS$ by subtracting the given measure of $\\angle QSP$ from 180 degrees:\n\n$$\\angle QRS = 180^\\circ - \\angle QSP = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ$$\n\nNow, we can find $\\angle PQR$ by remembering that $\\angle PQR$ and $\\angle QRS$ share a common side, and their angles add up to a straight angle (180 degrees). So we can set up the following equation:\n\n$$\\angle PQR + \\angle QRS = 180^\\circ$$\n\nAnd solve for $\\angle PQR$:\n\n$$\\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - \\angle QRS = 180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $\\angle PQR$ is $\\boxed{80^\\circ}$.",
